{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"regardable-superduper-whiteeye","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Cost Gerrit change 1942 (ticket silken-stealthful-narwhal) a spurious Verified -1: 1 failed, 14508 passed. The failure is unrelated to that change, which touches only scripts/gen_config_reference.py and tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nTEST: tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated\n\nFAILURE (run 32327846364, job 96302879852, ubuntu py3.13, xdist worker gw3):\n\n  shutil.Error: [('.../source/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock',\n                  '.../destination/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock',\n                  \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.../source/origin.git/objects/maintenance.lock'\")]\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe test pushes into the bare `source/origin.git` (line ~284, `git push -q origin HEAD:tickets`), which lets git kick off background auto-maintenance in that bare repo. Auto-maintenance takes a plain `$GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY/maintenance.lock` (gc.c, no pid/hostname/staleness — see ticket icicled-unstable-urial for the citation). The very next statement is `shutil.copytree(source_origin, destination_origin, symlinks=True)` (line ~295). copytree scandirs `objects/`, sees `maintenance.lock`, and by the time copy2 opens it the maintenance process has released and unlinked it, so copytree raises.\n\nThis is the SAME root-cause class already fixed for a different test in ticket chewed-illicit-blacklemur (bridge fsck keyset test, stray .git/objects/maintenance.lock on macOS). That fix did not generalise to this test.\n\n## Scope\n\n- tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py\n\n## Approach\n\nMake the copy immune to transient auto-maintenance artifacts rather than retrying: disable auto-maintenance for the repos the test creates (e.g. `git config maintenance.auto false` / `gc.auto 0` on `source_origin` before the push), and/or copy with an ignore predicate that skips `*.lock` under `objects/`. Prefer the config route: it removes the race instead of tolerating it. Then confirm the copy's isolation assertions still hold.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Reproduce deterministically by injecting a `maintenance.lock` into `source_origin/objects/` that is unlinked mid-walk, and assert the test still passes.\n- Re-run tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py repeatedly (>=20 iterations) with auto-maintenance enabled and observe zero failures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The transient `objects/*.lock` race can no longer fail the copy; checked by a deterministic reproduction that fails before the fix and passes after.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py -q` is green; checked by that command.\n- [ ] The fix removes the race rather than retrying it; checked by review of the diff for absence of retry/sleep loops.","id":"dca1-f641-caeb-4df4","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky: test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin races git auto-maintenance's objects/maintenance.lock"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787198160874259001,"uuid":"7f4b9ee7-1c9b-4354-9cbd-efbcc34e456d"}